{
  "mn114:0.1": "Middle Discourses 114 ",
  "mn114:0.2": "What Should and Should Not Be Cultivated ",
  "mn114:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn114:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn114:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn114:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn114:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn114:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn114:2.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you an exposition of the teaching on what should and should not be cultivated. ",
  "mn114:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn114:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn114:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn114:3.1": "“I say that there are two kinds of bodily behavior: ",
  "mn114:3.2": "that which you should cultivate, and that which you should not cultivate. ",
  "mn114:3.3": "And each of these is a kind of bodily behavior. ",
  "mn114:3.4": "I say that there are two kinds of verbal behavior: ",
  "mn114:3.5": "that which you should cultivate, and that which you should not cultivate. ",
  "mn114:3.6": "And each of these is a kind of verbal behavior. ",
  "mn114:3.7": "I say that there are two kinds of mental behavior: ",
  "mn114:3.8": "that which you should cultivate, and that which you should not cultivate. ",
  "mn114:3.9": "And each of these is a kind of mental behavior. ",
  "mn114:3.10": "I say that there are two arisings of thought: ",
  "mn114:3.11": "that which you shou